        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 1528,
        "area_px": 266050,
        "density": 0.00574,
        "chars": 132,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 86.39
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        477,
        2155,
        1376,
        3029
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Some reductions in congestion are also noted on the New York City subway lines serving lower Manhattan. Counts taken at three stations \u2014 the Wall Street stations of the East and West Side IRT and the BMT Broad Street Station \u2014 indicated that between 9 and 9:10 a.m. a total of 4620 passengers, about 6 percent of the usual number at that time, shifted into comparatively less congested earlier periods. It should be noted that 80 percent of the downtown employees are subway riders.",
